  description: Cadmium is a chemical element with symbol Cd and atomic number 48.
    This soft, bluish-white metal is chemically similar to the two other stable metals
    in group 12, zinc and mercury. Like zinc, it prefers oxidation state +2 in most
    of its compounds and like mercury it shows a low melting point compared to transition
    metals.
